     'e25d1e12b26e1eac52a2bca556e7170ea3dde4fa03ad53ed2bccec934c5f629b', 'Rice family = cooked white rice 130 (founder decision 4), copied from the verified row the 052 ''rice'' alias served (5f20d673, USDA FDC 168930), same numbers. Portions (founder 2026-11-13): 1 cup = 158 g, 1 katori = 130 g, 1 plate = 250 g on every rice key, replacing the US-cup 186 g. 5f20d673 itself is superseded (same_food_revised, numbers unchanged) so its key ''cooked white rice'' and its 052 aliases rice / white rice / steamed rice / chawal rice / chawal cooked rice follow it to a copy row with the new portions: 053 never edits a row in place, and leaving it verified would keep serving 186 g under that key and to every USDA 168930 match. Recalculated INDB boiled rice (117) is reported, not shipped. ''chawal'' (3 real entries, 2 users) becomes an exact key on its own copy row and its 052 alias retires: the fts resolver reads keys only, and once ''Boiled rice (Uble chawal)'' is quarantined its name search finds curd rice / rice kheer / sweet rice first (2026-11-13 review). ''chawal rice'' stays an 052 alias (ranked mode): a second key row would put two identical rice rows in every ranked ''X chawal'' list.', 'founder 2026-11-12'),
